=== PARITY (vs web PresetGallery.tsx) ===
  Data source -> useAutomationPresets(category) bound via the shared state-holder seam
    (PresetGallerySource -> PresetGalleryModel). The view performs NO HTTP. useNavigate ->
    the parent-supplied onInstall closure (web navigate('/automations/new?preset=${id}')).
    useTranslation -> P1/S10 PGStrings facade. useAutomations is the parent list-surface
    holder the same S8 layer feeds; this surface only needs the presets query.
  Projection -> PresetGalleryProjection.cards is a 1:1 port of `presets.map((p) => <PresetCard/>)`:
    stable key `preset.id`, the icon lookup `iconMap[preset.icon] ?? Shield` (eight SF-Symbol
    tokens + shield default), the first-trigger label `triggers[0] ? triggerLabels[kind] :
    noTrigger` (incl. the absent/unknown-kind fallback), and the action count `actions.length`.
  Composition -> each card mirrors the web GlassPanel(hover, glow=cyan): a cyan-tinted icon
    tile, the name + trigger subtitle, a neutral `{{count}} actions` badge (TSBadge look,
    facade-resolved), the 2-line description, and a secondary "Install" button (TSButton) with
    the plus glyph. The grid is TSFadeIn over a responsive LazyVGrid whose cells cascade with a
    TSStaggerItem delay (web FadeIn > StaggerContainer > StaggerItem). Recharts/Leaflet -> none.
  States (all render) ->
      loading -> a grid of FOUR skeleton cards (web `Array.from({length: 4})`);
      empty   -> a friendly ContentUnavailableView with the web clock glyph + message
                 (web `EmptyState`), never a blank box;
      error   -> the presets-query failure (TSQueryError equivalent + native retry -> refresh)
                 — the P4 treatment of the web hook's error (the leaf folds it into empty);
      presets -> the faithful web card grid;
      stale   -> a "Preset list may be out of date" chip + one auto-refresh per rising edge;
      offline -> an "Offline — showing cached presets" chip over the cached grid.
    Each state has a #if DEBUG preview + a unit test.
  i18n -> ALL EIGHT web-source t() keys resolve through the P1/S10 facade with the web English
    fallback (the 4 trigger labels + noTrigger + actionCount + install + empty), coverage 8/8;
    the i18next `{{count}}` interpolation is the native `%lld`. Plus 7 native chrome/a11y keys
    (empty message, loading, error, retry, stale, offline, install spoken label). No English
    literal in Swift (Text(verbatim:) over the facade; inline English lives only in PGText fallbacks).
  a11y -> each card body is one composed VoiceOver element (name, trigger, count, description);
    the Install control is a SEPARATE focusable element with a "Install {name}" label; the icon
    tile + count badge are hidden; the retry button + each status chip carry an accessibilityLabel;
    the loading grid is one labeled element; Dynamic Type via tokens; Reduce Motion gates the
    card hover lift, the FadeIn/stagger, and the TSSkeleton shimmer.
  Telemetry -> PresetGalleryModel.start() emits viewOpened(surface:"PresetGallery") -> bridges
    the shared Telemetry.track (P1/S11). Asserted by a spy test (fires exactly once, idempotent start).

